course: dictionary
lesson: 2457
title: A name with a capital letter
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Daniel is a proper noun. It is the name of one particular person, so it starts with a capital letter. «Daniel saw the chat that night and cried» is about one boy, the same way a name in a class list is about one child.
explain: In the Bible, Daniel is a prophet who stayed faithful to God. When the king's law forbade praying, Daniel kept praying anyway. He was thrown into a den of lions, but he came out unhurt. Lessons about courage and faith often tell this story.
explain: Context tells you which Daniel is meant. «Daniel explained that the king's kingdom would end» is about the Bible, because of the king and the wall. «In the class group chat in Vancouver someone posted a silly photo of Daniel» is about a boy. Read the words around the name and the clues decide.
fact: Daniel is a proper noun: it names one particular person, so it always starts with a capital letter.
fact: In the Bible, Daniel is a Jewish prophet who was taken to Babylon and stayed faithful to God.
fact: Daniel was thrown into a den of lions and came out unhurt.
fact: Daniel is also a common boy's first name, and it is often shortened to Dan or Danny.
fact: «The writing on the wall» now means a clear warning, and it comes from the Bible story of Daniel.
exercise: In «Daniel saw the chat that night and cried», what kind of word is Daniel? | A verb, a doing word | *A proper noun, the name of one person | An adjective, a describing word | A place name, like Vancouver
exercise: In the Bible, what happened to Daniel when he kept praying to God? | He was given a golden crown for stopping his prayers | He was sent home and never went back to Babylon | *He was thrown into a den of lions but came out unhurt | He was painted onto the palace wall
exercise: Which sentence uses Daniel as an ordinary boy's name? | *«Daniel was picked for the football team this week.» | «Daniel explained that the king's kingdom would end.» | «Daniel read the writing on the wall.» | «Daniel stayed faithful to God in Babylon.»
test: Why does Daniel start with a capital letter? | Because it is the first word of every sentence | Because it is a very long word | Because it is always written in bold | *Because it is a proper noun, the name of one particular person
test: Which two things can the name Daniel mean? | A town in Vancouver and a palace | A German scientist and a lion | *A Bible prophet and a common boy's first name | A king of Babylon and a golden statue
exam: In «Daniel explained that the king's kingdom would end», which clue tells you Daniel is the Bible prophet? | Vancouver | The word explained, which only ever means cried | *The king and the writing on the wall | The class group chat
